---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Ağustos Teknoloji"
  description="The publisher's house, the brand portfolio, and the rules that hold them together."
>
  <article class="container">
    <h1 class="type-h1">From the publisher's house</h1>
    <p class="type-body"><em>One symbol, five brands, and a typography that survives translation.</em></p>

    <p class="type-body">
      Ağustos is the parent. Beneath it sit a luminaire brand at mid-tier pricing,
      a publication archive of <em>PLD Türkiye</em>, a software tool for lighting data, and a
      newer house brand.
      Each carries the same mark and typography. Ağustos alone owns red as identity; the others are black and white. Shared red still marks links and interaction.
    </p>

    <h2 class="type-h2">The portfolio</h2>

    <dl class="type-dl">
      <dt>Ağustos Teknoloji</dt>
      <dd>Lighting agency and distribution. Red identity ink <code>#cf142a</code>.</dd>

      <dt>Pataraz</dt>
      <dd>Premium luminaire brand at mid-tier pricing. Neutral identity ink <code>#1a1a1a</code>.</dd>

      <dt>PLD Türkiye</dt>
      <dd>Lighting publication archive. Neutral identity ink <code>#1a1a1a</code>.</dd>

      <dt>IESdesk</dt>
      <dd>Software for working with lighting data. Neutral identity ink <code>#1a1a1a</code>.</dd>

      <dt>SpecQuick</dt>
      <dd>House brand. Neutral identity ink <code>#1a1a1a</code>.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2 class="type-h2">Six rules</h2>

    <ol>
      <li>Portability over preference.</li>
      <li>The publisher precedes the brand.</li>
      <li>One symbol, forever.</li>
      <li>Ağustos alone owns red as identity.</li>
      <li>Shared red signals links, focus, and small emphasis across the family.</li>
      <li>Turkish content declares its language.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="type-body">
      The full specification lives in <a href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DESIGN.md</a>,
      with the reasoning recorded in MEMORY.md. This site is its first implementation.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
